---
/**
 * THE INDEX — slice R8. The funnel spread, five destinations.
 *
 * CONTEXT.md Section Composition table, row "Index 01-05":
 *
 *   Entrance      Numerals already at display scale
 *   Column window 1-11
 *   Image         none
 *   Rhythm        standard
 *   Margin holds  — (empty)
 *   Length        index only
 *
 * THE ENTRANCE IS THE NUMERALS AND NOTHING IS ADDED ON TOP OF THEM.
 * No kicker, no hairline head, no visible section title, no decorative
 * mark, no photograph, no live-margin content. The table says the
 * entrance IS the numerals at display scale; an entrance device laid
 * over an entrance is two entrances.
 *
 * IT IS THE FIRST SECTION AFTER THE PIVOT. Everything above the
 * Feature Quote is her own work; everything below it is this. The
 * Index is the page's navigation, and it is the only section flush to
 * the sheet's left trim across its full width — see the window note in
 * the stylesheet for why that is what makes it read as a contents page
 * rather than as another section.
 *
 * ---- COPY -------------------------------------------------------
 * Verbatim from COPY.md, "Index". Five rows, in COPY.md's order:
 *
 *   01  Premier Leadership            Consulting & leadership development
 *   02  Everyday Legends Foundation   Education, athletics & service
 *   03  Educational Leadership        Alternative education high school principal
 *   04  The McClain Brothers          Jaylen, KJ & Cam
 *   05  Charging It to the Game       The blog
 *
 * THIS NUMBERING IS THE INDEX'S OWN. It is unrelated to page order, to
 * src/data/sections.ts's folio numerals, and to the decorative marks in
 * the abridged sections. CONTEXT.md's "Decorative marks vs. Index
 * numbers" rule: the three are unrelated typographic devices and MUST
 * NOT be made to agree. This has been flagged four times.
 *
 * ENTRY 01 READS "PREMIER LEADERSHIP", NOT "PREMIER LEADERSHIP, LLC".
 * The old build's FunnelIndex.astro carries the suffix; it does not
 * travel. COPY.md's resolved naming decision puts the legal form in
 * exactly one place on the site — the About paragraph, where the
 * client wrote it herself.
 *
 * THE UPPERCASE ON THE DESCRIPTIONS IS A text-transform, a visual
 * treatment. The authored strings are set in sentence case exactly as
 * COPY.md writes them, so a copy diff against the deck is a string
 * comparison and not a case-folding exercise.
 *
 * ---- DESTINATIONS -----------------------------------------------
 * 01/02/03 are outbound links, new tab, rel="noopener". NOT
 * "noopener noreferrer": anchor-digital-standards.md is the
 * authoritative cross-repo standard and noreferrer strips the Referer
 * header, costing Anchor referral attribution from every client site
 * it ships.
 *
 * 04 IS NOT A LINK. It is the <summary> of the expansion below it.
 *
 * 05 IS AN IN-PAGE ANCHOR, same tab, no rel. Its href is taken from
 * src/data/sections.ts rather than invented — the blog section's id in
 * that list is `charging-it-to-the-game`, so the anchor is
 * `#charging-it-to-the-game`. The section itself is R9 and does not
 * exist yet, so the anchor resolves to nothing today; that is expected
 * and is why the id is READ from the list rather than guessed. R9
 * mounts a <section> carrying that exact id.
 *
 * ---- THE EXPANSION IS NATIVE <details> --------------------------
 * NO JAVASCRIPT. No scroll listener, no observer, no toggle script, no
 * ARIA state management. <details>/<summary> handles aria-expanded
 * itself, and CONTEXT.md's "one scroll listener exists in the entire
 * build" budget is spent on the folio (R12), not on a disclosure.
 *
 * CLOSED ON LOAD. CONTEXT.md's "all content visible on load" rule is
 * about scroll-reveals and opacity-0 initial states — content that a
 * full-page capture or a client-generated PDF would render blank. The
 * three brothers are content behind a control the reader operates, not
 * content hidden from them, and the control announces itself. The old
 * build shipped `open` for the capture reason; that reasoning does not
 * survive the rule being read for what it is.
 *
 * ---- THE THREE BROTHERS -----------------------------------------
 * Data only, no prose. COPY.md gives three columns — name, program,
 * website — and three columns ship. No Instagram handle, no X handle,
 * no jersey graphic, no headshot, no class year beyond the one COPY.md
 * puts inside Cam's program string.
 *
 * ALL THREE DOMAINS ARE PLAIN TEXT, NOT LINKS. CONTEXT.md, Site
 * Structure: liveness is unconfirmed, and a dead click reads as a
 * broken site rather than as coming-soon while printed magazines are
 * driving traffic. Visual treatment is identical either way; only the
 * click is removed. They are NOT wrapped in <a>.
 *
 * OSU INTERIM RULE, ALL THREE SCHOOLS. School names as plain text
 * only. No logos, no marks, no team photography, no school-keyed
 * colour. Jaylen's 2026 Ohio State captaincy is NOT surfaced — the
 * client has made no public announcement.
 *
 * ---- NO GOLD ----------------------------------------------------
 * CONTEXT.md's gold budget, read as R7 left it: saturated type accents
 * are 3 of 3 and genuinely spent. The hairline-gold bucket reads 0 of
 * 8 — but 8 is a CEILING rather than a spend, and five rules in one
 * navigational section would consume most of that ceiling for the
 * page's least emphatic content. The Index's rules are Smoked Slate.
 * The old build's index drew every rule in gold; that does not travel
 * either.
 */
import { sections } from '../data/sections.ts';

/* The blog anchor is READ from the section list, never typed. If R9
   ships the blog under a different id, this breaks loudly at build
   time rather than shipping a silently dead anchor. */
const blog = sections.find((s) => s.label === 'Charging It to the Game');
if (!blog) {
  throw new Error(
    'R8: no "Charging It to the Game" entry in src/data/sections.ts — ' +
      'the Index cannot derive entry 05’s anchor.'
  );
}
const blogHref = `#${blog.id}`;
---

<section class="sheet index" id="sec-index" aria-labelledby="index-heading">
  {/* The section announces itself through the numerals and the rules,
      not through a title — so the <h2> is visually hidden via the .vh
      primitive (position:absolute + clip-path:inset(50%)), never
      display:none, which would take it out of the accessibility tree.
      The string matches this section's label in src/data/sections.ts
      exactly, per CONTEXT.md's locked heading structure: each
      section's <h2> is the same string the folio uses. */}
  <h2 class="vh" id="index-heading">Index</h2>

  {/* An <ol>, because the entries are an ordered list and the numerals
      are its numbering. The displayed numerals are authored text
      carrying aria-hidden="true": the list is ALREADY ordered, and
      "oh one" read before every name is noise. */}
  <ol class="idx-window idx-list">
    <li class="idx-item">
      <a
        class="idx-row"
        href="https://www.premierleadersllc.com"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
      >
        <span class="idx-num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <span class="idx-body">
          <span class="idx-line"><span class="idx-name">Premier Leadership</span></span>
          <span class="idx-desc">Consulting &amp; leadership development</span>
        </span>
      </a>
    </li>

    <li class="idx-item">
      <a
        class="idx-row"
        href="https://www.everydaylegend.com"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
      >
        <span class="idx-num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <span class="idx-body">
          <span class="idx-line"><span class="idx-name">Everyday Legends Foundation</span></span>
          <span class="idx-desc">Education, athletics &amp; service</span>
        </span>
      </a>
    </li>

    <li class="idx-item">
      <a class="idx-row" href="https://www.ucvts.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <span class="idx-num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <span class="idx-body">
          <span class="idx-line"><span class="idx-name">Educational Leadership</span></span>
          <span class="idx-desc">Alternative education high school principal</span>
        </span>
      </a>
    </li>

    {/* 04 — THE EXPANSION. The whole row is the <summary>; entry 04 is
        not a link. The rule that closes this entry sits on the <li>,
        BELOW the <details>, so it moves down when the expansion opens.
        That is correct: the rule closes the entry, not the summary. */}
    <li class="idx-item">
      <details class="idx-details">
        <summary class="idx-row">
          <span class="idx-num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <span class="idx-body">
            <span class="idx-line">
              <span class="idx-name">The McClain Brothers</span>
              {/* The indicator. Entry 04 is the only row carrying one —
                  it is the only row whose behaviour differs, and the
                  four link rows need no glyph to announce that they are
                  links. The glyph itself is generated content so the
                  +/- swap is a CSS state and not a script; the span is
                  aria-hidden because <details> already exposes
                  aria-expanded. NO rotation, NO transition, NO
                  transform. */}
              <span class="idx-sign" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </span>
            <span class="idx-desc">Jaylen, KJ &amp; Cam</span>
          </span>
        </summary>

        {/* Placed on .idx-body, so the brothers start on the same left
            edge as the names above them. NO sub-columns and NO new left
            edges — CONTEXT.md's three-edges rule holds inside this
            section as strictly as it holds outside it. */}
        <div class="idx-body idx-expand">
          <ul class="idx-bros">
            <li class="idx-bro">
              <span class="idx-bro-line">
                <span class="idx-bro-name">Jaylen McClain</span>
                <span class="idx-bro-site">jaylenmcclain.com</span>
              </span>
              <span class="idx-bro-prog">Ohio State Football | #8</span>
            </li>
            <li class="idx-bro">
              <span class="idx-bro-line">
                <span class="idx-bro-name">KJ McClain</span>
                <span class="idx-bro-site">kjmcclain.com</span>
              </span>
              <span class="idx-bro-prog">University of Tennessee Football | #40</span>
            </li>
            <li class="idx-bro">
              <span class="idx-bro-line">
                <span class="idx-bro-name">Cam McClain</span>
                <span class="idx-bro-site">cammcclain.com</span>
              </span>
              <span class="idx-bro-prog">Seton Hall Prep Football | #6 · Class of 2028</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </details>
    </li>

    <li class="idx-item">
      <a class="idx-row" href={blogHref}>
        <span class="idx-num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
        <span class="idx-body">
          <span class="idx-line"><span class="idx-name">Charging It to the Game</span></span>
          <span class="idx-desc">The blog</span>
        </span>
      </a>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

<style>
  /* ---- PADDING ---------------------------------------------------
     FLAT 110px TOP AND BOTTOM AT EVERY WIDTH, per CONTEXT.md's
     per-section table: Cover 64 · About 96 · Educational Leader 110 ·
     Premier 80 · Everyday Legends 70 · Athletic 110 · Feature Quote
     150 · INDEX 110 · Blog 110/40 · Contact 96. Sections MUST NOT
     share a padding token, so the value is set here and nowhere else.

     NO TAPER AND NO svh TERM. The pivot directly above carries a
     clamp — flat 150 in bands 1 and 2, clamp(116px, 14.67vw, 150px)
     below — and About carries a max(96px, 20svh + 12px). Neither
     reason applies here: the pivot's taper exists because 150px of
     padding around one line of type eats a phone viewport, and
     About's svh term exists to keep its lede below an 80svh Cover's
     fold. This section is five rows tall at every width and sits in
     the middle of the scroll. Flat 110, the same value Educational
     Leader and Athletic Management ship.

     NO min-height, NO svh, NO viewport-height floor of any kind
     (R1.4). */
  .index {
    padding-block: 110px;
  }

  /* ---- THE TYPE, AND EVERY AXIS -----------------------------------
     Fraunces defaults to wght 900, WONK ON and SOFT 100 when an axis
     is left unstated. Both tiers below enumerate all four, and
     `font-weight` restates the wght axis in the property the browser
     uses for fallback selection so a Fraunces-less render is not
     900-weight.

     WONK IS 0 ON BOTH. WONK 1 is spent at the Feature Quote and
     nowhere else — it is the pivot's flourish. Numerals set with
     flagged terminals would put the pivot's one signature on the
     page's navigation.

     These are new roles rather than existing --fx-* tiers: the
     numeral is a display-scale FIGURE, which wants opsz 96's sharp
     high-contrast register at wght 300 and SOFT 30, and the row name
     is a small-display role at opsz 24 / wght 400 / SOFT 60 — softer
     and more open than any existing tier, because it is read at 28px
     beside a 56px figure rather than seen alone. Declared locally so
     no other section inherits them.
     ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
  .index {
    --idx-num-size: clamp(36px, 3.9vw, 56px);
    --idx-num-lh: 1;

    --idx-name-size: clamp(20px, 1.95vw, 28px);
    --idx-name-lh: 1.15;

    --idx-desc-size: 11px;
    --idx-desc-lh: 1.6;
    /* The description's line box. Every internal gap in this section
       is a multiple of this or of the name's line box — never a fixed
       pixel value, per R3.1: "Derive internal gaps from the type, not
       from pixels. Fixed pixel gaps set from one width are a swept
       band by another name." */
    --idx-desc-line: calc(var(--idx-desc-size) * var(--idx-desc-lh));
  }

  .idx-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  /* ---- THE ROW ----------------------------------------------------
     ONE NUMERAL AND ONE TEXT BLOCK ON ONE BASELINE. The row is a
     subgrid of the section (see the primitive block in global.css) and
     carries `align-items: baseline`, so grid's own baseline-sharing
     group answers the alignment.

     THE OFFSET IS NOT MODELLED IN em. R6.3: Chrome rounds a font's
     ascent and descent to whole pixels at the rendered size, so a
     hand-written `lh/2 + (asc - desc)/2` offset drifts unpredictably
     with font-size — measured 0.02px out at 31.68px and 1.27px out at
     26px on this same face. The numeral runs from 36px to 56px across
     the page's widths and the name from 20px to 28px, so an em
     constant would be wrong at most of them. Baseline delta measured
     at 0.00px; see the pass report.

     VERTICAL PADDING IS DERIVED FROM THE DESCRIPTION'S LINE BOX, at
     1.15 of it. It is a calc() over the type tokens above, so moving
     the description's size or leading re-resolves every row's rhythm
     with nothing swept and no breakpoint band. */
  .idx-row {
    align-items: baseline;
    padding-block: calc(1.15 * var(--idx-desc-line));
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    /* Only opacity transitions anywhere in this section. Never
       transition-all, and never a colour transition — the hover
       states below are instant by specification. */
    transition: opacity 140ms var(--ease);
  }

  /* The whole row is the control on entry 04. The default disclosure
     marker comes off in both engines. */
  summary.idx-row {
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  summary.idx-row::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  /* ---- THE NUMERAL ------------------------------------------------
     Fraunces, opsz 96 · wght 300 · SOFT 30 · WONK 0. Obsidian.

     LEFT-ALIGNED INSIDE ITS WINDOW — never centred, never
     right-aligned. The window is three columns of twelve and the
     figures fill roughly a third of it; the air to their right is the
     leader space of a printed contents page and is deliberate. It is
     NOT closed by shrinking the window, which would put the text block
     on a fourth left edge.

     SCALE IS RELATIONAL, NOT ABSOLUTE. clamp(36px, 3.9vw, 56px)
     resolves to 56px at 1440 against a largest rendered lede of
     54.72px — a ratio of 1.02, inside the 0.90-1.15 window. The Index
     is the page's NAVIGATION; numerals set larger than the sections'
     own opening statements would invert the hierarchy. Against the row
     name it is 2.00x at 1440 and never falls below 1.80x at any width
     the page renders, both ends of the clamp included.

     `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` so 01-05 occupy identical
     advance widths — a contents column whose figures shift left and
     right by the width of a 1 is a contents column with five left
     edges. */
  .idx-num {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 96, 'wght' 300, 'SOFT' 30, 'WONK' 0;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: var(--idx-num-size);
    line-height: var(--idx-num-lh);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums;
    color: var(--obsidian);
  }

  /* ---- THE TEXT BLOCK ---------------------------------------------
     Its left edge is column 4 in the 12-column bands, which is the
     lede edge — one of CONTEXT.md's three established left edges.
     Nothing in this section lands on a fourth. */
  .idx-body {
    display: block;
  }

  /* The name's line. A flex row so the name and — on entry 04 only —
     the indicator share a baseline and the indicator right-aligns to
     THIS block's right edge rather than to an edge of its own. With
     one child (every row but 04) the name simply sits flush left and
     the flex container's first baseline is the name's, which is what
     the row's baseline group aligns the numeral to. Identical
     structure on all five rows, so all five baselines are computed the
     same way. */
  .idx-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--idx-desc-line);
  }

  /* Fraunces, opsz 24 · wght 400 · SOFT 60 · WONK 0. Obsidian. */
  .idx-name {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 24, 'wght' 400, 'SOFT' 60, 'WONK' 0;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--idx-name-size);
    line-height: var(--idx-name-lh);
    color: var(--obsidian);
  }

  /* Montserrat 11px / 500 / 0.14em / uppercase, Smoked Slate.

     THE UPPERCASE IS A text-transform. The authored string in the
     markup above is sentence case, exactly as COPY.md writes it.

     DESCRIPTIONS MAY WRAP. They are not the Athletic caption, which
     has to clear a three-column window on one line. A two-line
     description at 390 is correct behaviour, and the type is NOT
     shrunk and the tracking is NOT tightened to prevent it.

     The gap above is 0.30 of the NAME's line box, so it scales with
     the name across the clamp instead of holding one pixel value from
     one width — 9.66px at 1440, 6.90px at 390. */
  .idx-desc {
    display: block;
    margin-top: calc(0.3 * var(--idx-name-size) * var(--idx-name-lh));
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: var(--idx-desc-size);
    line-height: var(--idx-desc-lh);
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--slate);
  }

  /* ---- THE ROW HAIRLINES ------------------------------------------
     FOUR RULES, NOT FIVE AND NOT SIX. A bottom rule on entries 01, 02,
     03 and 04; NO rule under entry 05 and NO rule above entry 01. An
     index that opens and closes with a rule is a boxed table; one that
     only ever appears BETWEEN entries is a contents page.

     THE RULE IS ON THE <li>, NOT ON THE ROW. On entry 04 the <details>
     is inside the <li>, so the rule sits below the expansion and moves
     down when it opens. The rule closes the ENTRY, not the summary.

     1px Smoked Slate. NO GOLD — see the header comment. */
  .idx-item:not(:last-child) {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--slate);
  }

  /* ---- INTERACTIVE STATES -----------------------------------------
     Every clickable element gets hover, focus-visible and active.

     HOVER: the name takes a 1px underline and the row's hairline goes
     Obsidian. BOTH INSTANT — no colour transition anywhere. The
     hairline lives on the <li>, so the row's hover has to reach it
     through :has(); that is why the selector is shaped this way rather
     than sitting on .idx-row:hover.
     ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
  .idx-row:hover .idx-name {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  .idx-item:has(.idx-row:hover) {
    border-bottom-color: var(--obsidian);
  }

  .idx-row:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--slate);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .idx-row:active {
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* ---- THE INDICATOR ----------------------------------------------
     Montserrat + at description scale, Smoked Slate, right-aligned to
     the text block's right edge, becoming − (U+2212, the true minus,
     not a hyphen) under [open].

     NO ROTATION, NO TRANSITION, NO TRANSFORM. A rotating + is a
     component convention; this page is a printed spread and a printed
     spread's glyphs do not spin. The swap is a content change on a
     pseudo-element, which is why it needs no script.

     `flex-shrink: 0` so a long name never squeezes the glyph, and the
     span is aria-hidden — <details> already exposes aria-expanded and
     a screen reader announcing "plus" adds nothing. */
  .idx-sign {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: var(--idx-desc-size);
    line-height: var(--idx-desc-lh);
    color: var(--slate);
  }
  .idx-sign::before {
    content: '+';
  }
  .idx-details[open] .idx-sign::before {
    content: '\2212';
  }

  /* ---- THE EXPANSION ----------------------------------------------
     Data only, no prose. It sits on .idx-body, so it starts on the
     same left edge as the names — no sub-columns, no new left edges.

     THE GAP ABOVE THE FIRST BROTHER IS NOT THE GAP BETWEEN BROTHERS,
     AND THE FIRST ROUND SHIPPED IT AS ONE. The summary already carries
     its own 1.15-line bottom padding, and the brothers are 1.15 lines
     apart from each other, so with no padding here the expansion's
     first row sat exactly as far below "JAYLEN, KJ & CAM" as "KJ
     McClain" sits below Jaylen's program line — measured 37px against
     37px at 1440. Four items at one rhythm read as one list, and the
     description belongs to the SUMMARY, not to the brothers.

     0.62 lines on top of the summary's 1.15 makes the boundary 1.77
     lines against the list's own 1.15 — a 1.54:1 step, which is the
     smallest ratio that reads as a level change rather than as a
     slightly loose gap. Derived from the description's line box like
     every other gap in this section; nothing swept, no line count.

     The bottom gap stays at 1.15 lines, so the entry's rule closes the
     expansion at the same rhythm a closed row's rule closes it. */
  .idx-expand {
    padding-top: calc(0.62 * var(--idx-desc-line));
    padding-bottom: calc(1.15 * var(--idx-desc-line));
  }

  .idx-bros {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .idx-bro + .idx-bro {
    margin-top: calc(1.15 * var(--idx-desc-line));
  }

  /* Line 1: name left, domain right-aligned on the SAME LINE, sharing
     a baseline through flex's baseline alignment. The domain aligns to
     the text block's right edge — the one right-hand alignment this
     section permits, and it is an alignment to an edge that already
     exists rather than a new one.

     In bands 3 and 4 this becomes a block and the domain drops beneath
     the name; see the collapse block at the foot of this file. */
  .idx-bro-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--idx-desc-line);
  }

  .idx-bro-name {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--obsidian);
  }

  /* PLAIN TEXT, NOT A LINK, and not wrapped in an <a>. Liveness is
     unconfirmed and a dead click reads as a broken site. The visual
     treatment is what it would have been either way; only the click is
     removed. */
  .idx-bro-site {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: lowercase;
    color: var(--slate);
  }

  /* Line 2: the program. School names as plain text — the OSU interim
     rule is in force for all three schools: no logos, no marks, no
     team photography, no school-keyed colour. */
  .idx-bro-prog {
    display: block;
    margin-top: calc(0.3 * var(--idx-desc-line));
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--slate);
  }

  /* ---- BANDS 3 AND 4 ----------------------------------------------
     THE DOMAIN DROPS BENEATH THE NAME rather than right-aligning. At
     eight tracks the text block is five of eight — 556.5px at 1023 and
     421.4px at 751 — and "University of Tennessee Football | #40" plus
     "kjmcclain.com" on one line leaves a leader gap of a few
     characters, which reads as a failed justification rather than as
     an alignment. Below 750 there is one column and the question does
     not arise.

     Keyed at 1023 so it covers bands 3 and 4 together; there is no
     separate 750 rule, because a block is a block in both. */
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .idx-bro-line {
      display: block;
    }
    .idx-bro-site {
      display: block;
      margin-top: calc(0.2 * var(--idx-desc-line));
    }
  }

  /* Band 4 only. The numeral takes its own line above the text block
     — that is the grid primitive's doing, in global.css — and the two
     need a gap between them that the row's baseline group no longer
     provides once they are on separate rows. Derived from the
     numeral's own line box, not from a pixel. */
